      "evidence": "Transcribed from the raw HTML of North Yorkshire Council's live page 'Selective licensing in Scarborough Town from 1 June 2024', accordion section headed 'Scarborough town area 4: selective licensing street list'. The linked public legal notice on the same site (Housing Act 2004 ss.80-84, signed Nic Harne, Corporate Director) confirms the designation was made 23 January 2024, came into effect 1 June 2024 and ceases 31 May 2029, covering parts of Castle, Falsgrave and Stepney, and Northstead; the notice itself carries no street schedule, so the accordion list is the council's published schedule. CAUTION FOR MATCHING: seven entries are transcribed verbatim as the council writes them and each names two streets - 'Clarence Place and Clarence Road', 'Durham Street and Place', 'Falconers Road and Square', 'Market Street and Market Way', 'Marlborough Street and Terrace', 'Palace Hill and Palace Hill Lane', 'Pavilion Square and Terrace'; these were not split because the brief required no expansion. Appendix D of the May 2024 policy PDF carries an older 89-entry version lacking most number restrictions and naming 'Vernon Street (1-6)' where the live page says 'Vernon Road - 1 to 6'; the live council page was taken as the current authority."
